            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0348" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-12T15:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                                1924—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 12—1:55
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>10. Department’s 8, January 10, 5 p.m. Japanese authorities now state they have
                    no objection to visit to Tokyo of an officer to discuss details and technical
                    requirements of flight but as hitherto reported they do object to pathfinding
                    expedition described in Department’s instruction of July 18, 1923, and enclosure
                    from War Department dated July 5, which had been communicated to Foreign Office
                    on August 14th.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
